      "writtenOn": "2024-11-24T17:54:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@jaydenk from our discussion about the LE coc mtu configuration I remember that the maximum MTU needs to be provided by the offload stack to account for limitations in memory; that same limit will also apply to RFCOMM, and there is no reason why it should be different (give or take the RFC header bytes).",
      "parentUuid": "a25e1427_cd84c012",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "dde33f2109c44206e2918231638781124aa520dd",
