    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "04d6911a_866eec0b",
        "filename": "bluetooth/socket/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/socket/RfcommChannelInfo.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 66,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-22T22:10:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do you know how the maximum frame size is currently configured for RFCOMM ?\nIs there a relation to the MTU for the L2CAP channel or is it independent ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 66,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 66,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "dde33f2109c44206e2918231638781124aa520dd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8ead0491_f28e514a",
        "filename": "bluetooth/socket/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/socket/RfcommChannelInfo.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 66,
      "author": {
        "id": 1959861
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-22T22:44:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently, socket layer sets 990 bytes for RFCOMM max frame size.\n\n```\n#define BTA_JV_DEF_RFC_MTU (3 * 330)\n\n  if (RFCOMM_CreateConnectionWithSecurity(UUID_SERVCLASS_SERIAL_PORT, remote_scn, false, BTA_JV_DEF_RFC_MTU, peer_bd_addr, \u0026handle, bta_jv_port_mgmt_cl_cback, sec_mask)\n```\n\nThen, RFCOMM layer (port_api.cc) find minimum MTU between the input RFCOMM max frame size (3*330) and max L2CAP MTU (1691-1). The default socket RFCOMM max frame size is smaller so that 990 bytes has been used for RFCOMM socket for now.\n\nIn below code, `mtu` is 990 bytes socket layer configured. `rfcomm_mtu` is the calculated L2CAP MTU for RFCOMM based on hard-coded value.\n\n```\n  // Find MTU\n  // If the MTU is not specified (0), keep MTU decision until the PN frame has\n  // to be send at that time connection should be established and we will know\n  // for sure our prefered MTU\n  uint16_t rfcomm_mtu \u003d L2CAP_MTU_SIZE - RFCOMM_DATA_OVERHEAD;\n  if (mtu) {\n    p_port-\u003emtu \u003d (mtu \u003c rfcomm_mtu) ? mtu : rfcomm_mtu;\n  } else {\n    p_port-\u003emtu \u003d rfcomm_mtu;\n  }\n```\n\nSo, it sounds like RFCOMM max frame size will not larger than the calculated L2CAP MTU.",
      "parentUuid": "04d6911a_866eec0b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 66,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 66,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "dde33f2109c44206e2918231638781124aa520dd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c9ff57dd_a0c4f26e",
        "filename": "bluetooth/socket/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/socket/RfcommChannelInfo.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 66,
      "author": {
        "id": 1959861
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-23T00:30:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In host stack implementation, there is relation to the hard-coded MTU of L2CAP as 1685 bytes (\u003d 1691 - 6). RFCOMM max frame size could be capped by the L2CAP MTU but socket layer already configured smaller 990 bytes so that 990 bytes has been used. Anyway, we need `maxFrameSize` field in RfcommChannelInfo.aidl",
      "parentUuid": "8ead0491_f28e514a",
